From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netifd: let protocols retire their host dependency watches

After successfully applying a complete live configuration, a protocol can
retire its previous dependency watches and publish its current endpoints.
Require the current setup token and reject retired teardown/abort owners.

This retires only the protocol's watches. It does not delete netifd's shared
underlay host-route cache or change another protocol's route lifetime.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

--- a/proto-ext.c
+++ b/proto-ext.c
@@ -788,6 +788,14 @@ proto_ext_notify(struct interface_proto_
 		return proto_ext_add_host_dependency(state, tb);
 	case 7:
 		return proto_ext_setup_failed(state);
+	case 8:
+		/* A successful in-place update republishes its complete dependency
+		 * set. Retire old watches only once the protocol is ready to do so.
+		 */
+		if (!tb[NOTIFY_TOKEN] || state->sm == S_TEARDOWN || state->sm == S_SETUP_ABORT)
+			return UBUS_STATUS_PERMISSION_DENIED;
+		proto_ext_clear_host_dep(state);
+		return 0;
 	default:
 		return UBUS_STATUS_INVALID_ARGUMENT;
 	}
